> f(x: real) = sqrt(log(x))
> domain f
domain of f:
  x: real (default [-10, 10])
  requires log(x) >= 0
  requires x > 0
  defined on (numerically, grid of 20001 over [-10, 10]):
    x in [1, 10]
> range f
range of f:
  [0, 1.517427129]   min at x ≈ 1, max at x ≈ 10
  undefined at 11000 of 20001 grid points
  grid of 20001 points over [-10, 10] (default; give x a range), extrema refined at critical points
> g(x: real) = 1/sqrt(x)
> domain g
domain of g:
  x: real (default [-10, 10])
  requires sqrt(x) != 0  (in 1/sqrt(x))
  requires x >= 0
  defined on (numerically, grid of 20001 over [-10, 10]):
    x in (0, 10]
    except x ≈ 0  (sqrt(x) = 0)
> range g
range of g:
  [0.316227766, 31.6227766]   min at x ≈ 10, max at x ≈ 0.001
  undefined at 10001 of 20001 grid points
  grid of 20001 points over [-10, 10] (default; give x a range), extrema refined at critical points
> h(x: real) = sqrt(1 - x^2)
> domain h
domain of h:
  x: real (default [-10, 10])
  requires 1 - x^2 >= 0
  defined on (numerically, grid of 20001 over [-10, 10]):
    x in [-1, 1]
> range h
range of h:
  [0, 1]   min at x ≈ -1, max at x ≈ 0
  undefined at 18000 of 20001 grid points
  grid of 20001 points over [-10, 10] (default; give x a range), extrema refined at critical points
